{"name":"Peyote","hex":"#c5bbae","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"peyote","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small, spineless cactus (Lophophora williamsii) found from southwest United States to central Mexico that produces buttonlike tubercles that can be chewed for their psychedelic effect, primarily from the drug mescaline.","A mescal button produced by the plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peyote"}],"entries":[{"title":"Peyote","blocks":[{"text":"Peyote, also known as Lophophora williamsii, is a small, spineless cactus which contains psychoactive alkaloids, particularly mescaline. Peyote is a Spanish word derived from the Nahuatl peyōtl, meaning \"caterpillar cocoon\", from a root peyōni, \"to glisten\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Peyote_Cactus.jpg/330px-Peyote_Cactus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peyote","wikidata":"Q271937"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Lophophora_williamsii_ies.jpg/500px-Lophophora_williamsii_ies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Lophophora_williamsii_ies.jpg/500px-Lophophora_williamsii_ies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A group of Lophophora williamsii","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALophophora_williamsii_ies.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Lophophora_williamsii.jpg/500px-Lophophora_williamsii.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Lophophora_williamsii.jpg/1280px-Lophophora_williamsii.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/co